## Findings

Starting position retained but narrowed: rodent deletion may establish an endogenous cis requirement for steady-state first-exon RNA, even without proving altered initiation. This is stronger than a reporter but weaker than the requested nascent/state/dosage-controlled mechanism.

Before reading new numerical outcomes, selected discriminating prediction: precise perturbation of a verified Pmp22 cis element reduces calibrated P1-associated nascent synthesis relative to P2 before a broad differentiation response. Same-donor non-targeting/safe-harbor editing is the negative intervention control; Mpz and a prespecified differentiation/proliferation panel are state controls. P2 is a specificity comparator, not an assumed unchanged negative control. Failure of nascent change with mature first-exon RNA change leaves RNA fate viable. GSE139321's chronic trans SOX10 knockout and three-day cAMP differentiation cannot directly test this prediction even if its cluster expression is measurable. Numerical cluster review will be retrospective source verification, not a new locked biological test.

New primary-source audit changes the blanket human limitation: PMC7145652 includes endogenous TATA-box editing in commercial primary human Schwann cells (Figure 1) with total PMP22 RT-qPCR after seven-day differentiation. Promoter-specific human P1 versus P2 RT-qPCR is reported in a DIFFERENT context: pooled C22-mouse Schwann cultures bearing human transgenes (Supplementary Figure S2, main text). Therefore human endogenous cis perturbation is not wholly absent, but endogenous human promoter-selective initiation is not demonstrated by combining these two contexts. No donor independence or unchanged locus copy number is assumed. C22 pools are 6–10 mice/preparation, not individual biological replicates.

PMC6482019 RUNX cis-site deletion increases total Pmp22 in mouse NF1-deficient clones (Figure 4); the promoter-specific P1 result belongs to Runx1/3 trans-factor knockout tumors/sorted cells (Figure 5), not the same cis-edited clones. Do not fuse those assays into a cis-specific P1 necessity claim. The literal source P2 token ENSMUST0000001836 appears malformed and will be retained, flagged and not silently repaired.

